 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Two mechanisms make `request`, `session` and `g` available in templates:\n\n**1. Jinja globals (all templates, including imported ones)**\n- `Tessel.create_jinja_environment()` in `src/tessel/app.py:467` calls `rv.globals.update(...)` with `request`, `session`, `g`, plus `config`, `link_for` and `get_flashed_messages`. These are the `LocalProxy` objects from `src/tessel/globals.py`.\n\n**2. Default context injector (at render time)**\n- `_base_template_vars()` in `src/tessel/templating.py:21` is pre-registered in `Scaffold.template_ctx_injectors[None]` (`src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:184`).\n- It replaces `g` and `request` with the concrete objects from the app context, for speed. `session` stays a proxy so that access is tracked.\n- `render_template`, `render_template_string` and the `stream_*` variants (via `_render` and `_stream` in `src/tessel/templating.py`) call `Tessel.fill_template_scope()` (`src/tessel/app.py:588`).\n- That method runs the injectors for the app (`None`) and then for the request's bundles. Values passed to `render_template` take precedence over the injected ones.\n\n**Adding your own variables**\n- Use the `@app.ctx_injector` decorator, defined in `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:550`. It is available on both app and bundle objects. Decorate a function that returns a dict, and its keys become template variables.\n- On a bundle, `@bundle.ctx_injector` only applies to templates rendered from that bundle's views. To make it apply to every template, use `@bundle.app_ctx_injector` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:645`).\n- For static values, functions or filters, you can also add to `app.jinja_env.globals` directly. `src/tessel/sansio/app.py:825` shows the existing global-registration path.",
